1
00:01:16,682 --> 00:01:19,161
At last, today's main event is about to begin!

2
00:01:19,185 --> 00:01:21,764
Here's 250-pound Super Kong of the Dragon's Lair

3
00:01:21,788 --> 00:01:24,166
with 5 wins and one loss.

4
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:26,769
Listen to him roar! What a monster!

5
00:01:26,793 --> 00:01:30,773
The challenger from the Tiger's Lair
debuts in this match today!

6
00:01:30,797 --> 00:01:34,777
He is Gold Tiger Mask,
also known as the Yellow Devil.

7
00:01:34,801 --> 00:01:38,680
Will he emerge victorious from his debut match?

8
00:01:38,704 --> 00:01:40,349
Or will he become the latest victim

9
00:01:40,373 --> 00:01:42,751
of Super Kong's win streak?

10
00:01:42,775 --> 00:01:44,553
A one fall match with no time limit!

11
00:01:44,577 --> 00:01:47,569
A hair-raising battle is set to begin!

12
00:02:47,286 --> 00:02:49,380
A barrage of kicks and punches!

13
00:02:50,389 --> 00:02:52,968
Both sides look sharp!

14
00:02:52,992 --> 00:02:56,986
However, Gold Tiger Mask
seems to have a slight edge.

15
00:02:57,196 --> 00:02:58,673
Or not!

16
00:02:58,697 --> 00:03:01,496
Super Kong unleashes a roar of wrath!

17
00:03:06,305 --> 00:03:08,984
"10 years ago"

18
00:03:08,951 --> 00:03:10,942
"Children's Home"

19
00:03:12,154 --> 00:03:13,932
Everybody, gather round!

20
00:03:13,956 --> 00:03:16,634
Make two lines starting here.

21
00:03:16,658 --> 00:03:19,804
Older kids, take care of the younger ones.

22
00:03:19,828 --> 00:03:21,906
Does everyone have their booklets?

23
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:23,608
Yes...

24
00:03:23,632 --> 00:03:27,212
All right, then. Let's go!

25
00:03:27,236 --> 00:03:28,213
Naoto?

26
00:03:28,237 --> 00:03:31,416
Ruriko, what's the matter?

27
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:35,434
Naoto. Hurry up, or you'll be left behind.

28
00:03:38,747 --> 00:03:43,628
Look! Elephants! They're huge!

29
00:03:43,652 --> 00:03:45,848
Over there too! See?

30
00:03:47,156 --> 00:03:51,136
They are big, aren't they?

31
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:53,026
Take a good look, okay?

32
00:03:58,634 --> 00:04:00,712
Naoto!

33
00:04:00,736 --> 00:04:01,813
Naoto.

34
00:04:01,837 --> 00:04:05,116
Where have you been?

35
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,318
Mommy! Daddy!

36
00:04:07,304 --> 00:04:08,982
Thank goodness!

37
00:04:09,006 --> 00:04:10,784
Don't take off like that.

38
00:04:10,808 --> 00:04:13,106
Let's go.
Okay.

39
00:04:32,396 --> 00:04:34,074
What's the matter?

40
00:04:34,098 --> 00:04:35,375
Nothing.

41
00:04:35,399 --> 00:04:38,779
You're lying. It's all over your face.

42
00:04:38,648 --> 00:04:41,426
You too, Ruriko.

43
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:43,428
Meaning what?

44
00:04:43,452 --> 00:04:48,133
I don't want to get kicked out of
this Children's Home.

45
00:04:48,157 --> 00:04:52,638
So, you know that the property manager came?

46
00:04:52,662 --> 00:04:55,741
I am so sorry!

47
00:04:55,765 --> 00:05:00,327
Mr. Wakatsuki, I didn't come here for apologies.

48
00:05:05,541 --> 00:05:08,135
Read this.

49
00:05:11,047 --> 00:05:15,727
If you can't pay, you must move out.
It's in the lease.

50
00:05:15,751 --> 00:05:19,431
I'm doing my best to cut costs
as much as possible.

51
00:05:19,455 --> 00:05:21,633
As I explained before...

52
00:05:21,657 --> 00:05:25,537
this is an orphanage
that relies solely on donations.

53
00:05:25,561 --> 00:05:28,340
A field trip tomorrow?

54
00:05:28,364 --> 00:05:31,944
You should pay rent first, don't you think?

55
00:05:31,968 --> 00:05:36,415
It's the only trip we go on every year.

56
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:38,517
Our children look forward to this.

57
00:05:38,541 --> 00:05:42,535
Well, we are taking legal actions now.

58
00:05:42,645 --> 00:05:45,324
Please! If you could ask the landlord

59
00:05:45,348 --> 00:05:48,527
to give us one more month...

60
00:05:48,551 --> 00:05:52,545
We've already done this three times!

61
00:05:52,755 --> 00:05:54,933
We can't do this anymore!

62
00:05:54,957 --> 00:05:57,836
Please! I'm begging you!

63
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:02,559
For the love of God, Mr. Kinoshita!

64
00:06:04,166 --> 00:06:08,513
The children have nowhere else to go.

65
00:06:08,537 --> 00:06:13,218
This is their only home.

66
00:06:13,242 --> 00:06:15,020
I'm begging you!

67
00:06:15,044 --> 00:06:16,922
I can't do anything.

68
00:06:16,946 --> 00:06:18,846
Please!

69
00:06:36,565 --> 00:06:40,524
If I were strong enough, I'd beat him up.

70
00:06:41,937 --> 00:06:44,816
I wish my mom was still alive.

71
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:48,242
I guess we won't be able to stay together.

72
00:06:52,448 --> 00:06:54,041
Hey.

73
00:06:57,353 --> 00:06:58,930
This is for you.

74
00:06:58,954 --> 00:07:01,355
Take it.

75
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,360
That way, you will always remember me.

76
00:07:10,466 --> 00:07:11,543
I'll remember you!

77
00:07:11,567 --> 00:07:13,433
Just keep it.

78
00:07:20,543 --> 00:07:21,942
Naoto?

79
00:07:26,716 --> 00:07:29,208
What's the matter?

80
00:07:33,523 --> 00:07:35,423
Date Naoto.

81
00:07:37,927 --> 00:07:41,921
Come with me. And you'll be strong.

82
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:46,894
You have special power.

83
00:07:50,506 --> 00:07:52,484
Naoto?

84
00:07:52,454 --> 00:07:54,548
Naoto, where are you going?

85
00:08:07,770 --> 00:08:09,966
Who are you, mister?

86
00:08:17,279 --> 00:08:21,226
If you could have one wish granted...

87
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:23,651
Name one.

88
00:08:25,854 --> 00:08:27,932
To be strong.

89
00:08:27,956 --> 00:08:31,036
I don't want to be alone again.

90
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:35,040
I see. Then come with me.

91
00:08:35,064 --> 00:08:37,863
To where?

92
00:08:39,429 --> 00:08:40,906
To the Tiger's Lair.

93
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:43,809
Naoto...

94
00:08:43,833 --> 00:08:45,411
Dad! Akira!
What happened?

95
00:08:45,435 --> 00:08:47,713
Naoto is gone!

96
00:08:47,737 --> 00:08:51,617
Naoto...

97
00:08:51,641 --> 00:08:53,686
Naoto's missing!
Naoto...

98
00:08:53,710 --> 00:08:54,987
Naoto!

99
00:08:55,011 --> 00:08:57,590
Naoto...

100
00:08:57,614 --> 00:08:59,492
Are you listening?

101
00:08:59,516 --> 00:09:01,193
Sorry. What is it?

102
00:09:01,217 --> 00:09:04,296
<i>Were you recruited by Mr. %, too?</i>

103
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,600
Yeah, I was. You too, Dan?

104
00:09:07,624 --> 00:09:11,604
I think everyone here has been.

105
00:09:11,628 --> 00:09:16,509
In your case, he just had pity on you.

106
00:09:16,533 --> 00:09:21,013
What's his problem?

107
00:09:21,037 --> 00:09:23,416
You don't want to talk to him.

108
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,817
How come?

109
00:09:24,841 --> 00:09:29,288
He burned his family's house down.

110
00:09:29,312 --> 00:09:31,406
Shut your mouth!

111
00:09:35,218 --> 00:09:39,212
He wouldn't have a place to go back to, then.

112
00:09:44,327 --> 00:09:47,306
Get off, you brats!

113
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:49,128
Come on! Move it!

114
00:09:52,936 --> 00:09:55,815
This whip is for lazy bums!

115
00:09:55,839 --> 00:09:58,137
Hurry up, already!

116
00:10:06,961 --> 00:10:09,340
Move.

117
00:10:09,364 --> 00:10:11,458
Follow me.

118
00:10:28,862 --> 00:10:31,058
Hurry up and walk!

119
00:10:45,045 --> 00:10:47,139
We're here,

120
00:10:49,149 --> 00:10:53,143
This is your new home. The Tiger's Lair.

121
00:11:25,552 --> 00:11:27,646
Line up!

122
00:12:08,362 --> 00:12:10,456
Single file!

123
00:12:26,327 --> 00:12:29,306
Welcome to the Tiger's Lair.

124
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:32,231
There's no reason to fear.

125
00:12:35,916 --> 00:12:39,596
You should consider yourselves lucky.

126
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:44,300
You've been selected as part of this family.

127
00:12:44,324 --> 00:12:48,872
I will be your father and...

128
00:12:48,896 --> 00:12:51,297
your mentor too.

129
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:58,202
You have older brothers. They arrived before you.

130
00:13:00,868 --> 00:13:05,248
Follow the teachings of the Tiger's Lair,

131
00:13:05,272 --> 00:13:07,172
and this is what you'll become.

132
00:13:19,653 --> 00:13:24,534
They are the greatest fighters on Earth.

133
00:13:24,558 --> 00:13:27,357
They have trained for years...

134
00:13:28,862 --> 00:13:32,742
to become absolutely unbeatable.

135
00:13:32,766 --> 00:13:38,348
A glorious future awaits only those

136
00:13:38,372 --> 00:13:40,466
who endure harsh training.

137
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:46,829
These are no ordinary masks.

138
00:13:46,853 --> 00:13:50,633
It took me years to perfect these Tiger Masks.

139
00:13:50,657 --> 00:13:55,204
These masks are capable of unlocking

140
00:13:55,228 --> 00:13:57,629
the wearer's deepest potential beyond his limit.

141
00:14:00,834 --> 00:14:03,813
The white one unleashes power.

142
00:14:03,837 --> 00:14:05,931
The gold one enhances speed.

143
00:14:08,041 --> 00:14:14,524
And the one that is superior
to both in every aspect is...

144
00:14:14,515 --> 00:14:16,813
this black Tiger Mask.

145
00:14:21,121 --> 00:14:23,800
Complete the arduous training here.

146
00:14:23,824 --> 00:14:26,569
If you are deemed worthy,

147
00:14:26,593 --> 00:14:29,085
you will have the honor of
wearing one of the masks.

148
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,678
Listen carefully.

149
00:14:35,702 --> 00:14:38,782
Train hard and...

150
00:14:38,806 --> 00:14:43,710
embody the soul of the beast in your body.

151
00:14:45,212 --> 00:14:48,591
Strive for a strength...

152
00:14:48,552 --> 00:14:51,954
That no man can defeat!

153
00:14:54,959 --> 00:14:58,805
Here are the commandments of the Tiger's Lair.

154
00:14:58,829 --> 00:15:01,308
Repeat after me.

155
00:15:01,332 --> 00:15:04,011
Yes, madam...

156
00:15:04,035 --> 00:15:08,315
First, mercy is for the weak.

157
00:15:08,339 --> 00:15:12,333
First, mercy is for the weak...

158
00:15:12,443 --> 00:15:16,423
Second, fairness is the excuse of fools.

159
00:15:16,447 --> 00:15:21,128
Second, fairness is the excuse of fools...

160
00:15:21,152 --> 00:15:26,833
And finally, what is the reason why we fight?

161
00:15:26,857 --> 00:15:29,236
For the glory of the Tiger's Lair!

162
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,438
For the glory of the Tiger's Lair...

163
00:15:31,462 --> 00:15:32,406
Once again!

164
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:36,710
First, mercy is for the weak...

165
00:15:36,734 --> 00:15:41,415
Second, fairness is the excuse of fools...

166
00:15:41,439 --> 00:15:43,517
What do we fight for?

167
00:15:43,541 --> 00:15:46,340
For the glory of the Tiger's Lair...

168
00:16:48,134 --> 00:16:50,535
You could get yourselves killed!

169
00:17:23,235 --> 00:17:26,314
A weak man can't survive.

170
00:17:26,245 --> 00:17:29,943
That's the fate for those who live here.

171
00:17:42,962 --> 00:17:45,624
Good job today, everyone.

172
00:17:56,642 --> 00:18:00,222
I prepared this special dinner
with the greatest care.

173
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:01,724
Here are the perfect meal

174
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:04,226
and dietary supplements for your needs.

175
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:08,244
Don't be picky. Eat it all.

176
00:18:09,255 --> 00:18:10,833
Stop it.

177
00:18:10,857 --> 00:18:14,236
Just give me your meat.

178
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:17,339
All right.

179
00:18:17,363 --> 00:18:18,607
Here you go.

180
00:18:18,591 --> 00:18:21,270
Don't mess with me!

181
00:18:21,294 --> 00:18:23,272
Who do you think I am?

182
00:18:23,296 --> 00:18:25,274
I'll wear the black Tiger someday.

183
00:18:25,298 --> 00:18:27,096
You little turd!

184
00:18:32,305 --> 00:18:34,205
Come on.

185
00:18:36,109 --> 00:18:38,203
Why, you!

186
00:18:39,612 --> 00:18:42,206
Boys, stop it!

187
00:18:45,118 --> 00:18:48,418
Calm down!

188
00:18:53,693 --> 00:18:56,492
Come get me!

189
00:19:02,301 --> 00:19:03,879
You two! Stop!

190
00:19:03,903 --> 00:19:05,598
Let go of me!

191
00:19:07,607 --> 00:19:09,701
I said, stop!

192
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:12,908
Stop!

193
00:19:23,046 --> 00:19:26,016
A deadly attack, the Tiger's Lair Plug.

194
00:19:37,227 --> 00:19:39,628
Stop, do you not understand?

195
00:19:43,934 --> 00:19:47,131
I must ask Mr. X to punish you.

196
00:19:53,744 --> 00:19:56,441
Remember, you'll pay for this.

197
00:20:01,618 --> 00:20:03,017
Line up.

198
00:20:05,322 --> 00:20:07,800
Still have energy to fight each other?

199
00:20:07,617 --> 00:20:10,712
I'll make a point of working you harder tomorrow.

200
00:20:21,031 --> 00:20:26,128
Fighting among brothers is not allowed here.

201
00:20:39,416 --> 00:20:41,294
You are the smallest

202
00:20:41,318 --> 00:20:43,696
and you still thought you could stop the fight?

203
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,298
If Maki hadn't stepped in,

204
00:20:45,322 --> 00:20:48,301
you would have been crushed.

205
00:20:48,325 --> 00:20:50,503
I had to help my friend, sir.

206
00:20:50,527 --> 00:20:55,107
Mercy is for the weak.

207
00:20:55,131 --> 00:20:57,410
The strong one always wins

208
00:20:57,434 --> 00:21:00,413
and the winner is always right.

209
00:21:00,437 --> 00:21:03,416
Don't ever forget that.

210
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:07,206
Winning is the priority
over anything and everything.

211
00:21:13,917 --> 00:21:16,796
But remember...

212
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:20,222
there are two types of strength.

213
00:21:24,027 --> 00:21:25,722
The strength here and...

214
00:21:29,633 --> 00:21:32,125
The strength here.

215
00:21:37,941 --> 00:21:39,785
Strengthen here.

216
00:21:39,809 --> 00:21:43,404
And you'll be stronger than any other man.

217
00:22:02,532 --> 00:22:04,728
Jo!

218
00:22:08,638 --> 00:22:11,217
Don't look down!

219
00:22:11,241 --> 00:22:15,109
Keep your eyes up and pull yourself upward!

220
00:22:35,932 --> 00:22:38,010
Why didn't you save him?

221
00:22:38,034 --> 00:22:40,526
One less competitor to worry about.

222
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:47,987
Mercy is for the weak. Repeat it.

223
00:22:48,011 --> 00:22:51,791
Mercy is for the weak...

224
00:22:51,815 --> 00:22:53,392
Repeat it.

225
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:56,818
Mercy is for the weak.

226
00:23:16,339 --> 00:23:18,084
Oh, it's you, Dan.

227
00:23:18,108 --> 00:23:21,187
I was getting worried about you.

228
00:23:21,211 --> 00:23:25,891
I wonder if I should've saved him.

229
00:23:25,915 --> 00:23:27,493
It's not your fault.

230
00:23:27,517 --> 00:23:31,010
If you tried to help, you would've fallen too.

231
00:23:32,622 --> 00:23:36,502
Are we supposed to keep going on like this?

232
00:23:36,526 --> 00:23:39,018
We must follow the commandments,

233
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:45,911
First, mercy is for the weak!

234
00:23:45,935 --> 00:23:49,929
Second, fairness is the excuse of fools!

235
00:23:51,808 --> 00:23:53,986
And what do we fight for?

236
00:23:53,954 --> 00:23:56,753
For the glory of the Tiger's Lair!

237
00:24:13,374 --> 00:24:14,951
Listen.

238
00:24:14,975 --> 00:24:16,953
We train not only your body,

239
00:24:16,977 --> 00:24:19,071
but also your mind here.

240
00:24:23,784 --> 00:24:26,329
Study the cycle of the flames,

241
00:24:26,353 --> 00:24:28,531
and get to the other side.

242
00:24:28,555 --> 00:24:31,735
No one at your level

243
00:24:31,759 --> 00:24:34,838
has ever passed this challenge.

244
00:24:34,862 --> 00:24:38,856
Does anyone dare to give it a try?

245
00:25:06,316 --> 00:25:09,308
Enough. Back in line.

246
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:16,993
Next?

247
00:25:31,883 --> 00:25:33,476
Naoto!

248
00:26:35,303 --> 00:26:36,896
Way to go!

249
00:27:07,802 --> 00:27:12,350
Dan, Jo, and Naoto.

250
00:27:12,374 --> 00:27:17,555
10 years have passed since you arrived here.

251
00:27:17,579 --> 00:27:22,159
You three have survived and proven yourselves

252
00:27:22,183 --> 00:27:24,379
worthy of the title of Tiger Mask.

253
00:27:50,832 --> 00:27:54,211
Receiving the honor of the Mask

254
00:27:54,235 --> 00:27:56,135
does not mean the end of the training.

255
00:27:58,139 --> 00:28:00,335
He seems relaxed and confident.

256
00:28:02,844 --> 00:28:06,838
At this very moment,

257
00:28:07,048 --> 00:28:10,348
anew chapter of your destiny has begun.

258
00:30:30,410 --> 00:30:32,655
The main event is about to start!

259
00:30:32,679 --> 00:30:35,958
The Black Tiger Mask versus the Salamander!

260
00:30:35,982 --> 00:30:38,361
This is the debut match for the Black Tiger.

261
00:30:38,385 --> 00:30:40,763
His potential is unknown.

262
00:30:40,787 --> 00:30:43,766
His first opponent is pretty tough!

263
00:30:43,790 --> 00:30:45,868
Here comes the Salamander,

264
00:30:45,892 --> 00:30:48,088
unbeaten champion, from the Dragon Cave.

265
00:31:00,364 --> 00:31:02,442
He is known for his unparalleled ruthlessness.

266
00:31:02,466 --> 00:31:04,410
He'd do anything to win!

267
00:31:04,434 --> 00:31:07,413
He seems relaxed and confident.

268
00:31:07,437 --> 00:31:09,315
He's so confident that

269
00:31:09,339 --> 00:31:11,831
he's already doing his victory dance.

270
00:31:19,049 --> 00:31:20,827
He boasts ten out of ten victories.

271
00:31:20,851 --> 00:31:23,429
He is the greatest!

272
00:31:23,453 --> 00:31:28,434
The flame is bigger and stronger than ever!

273
00:31:28,458 --> 00:31:31,553
And there goes the bell!

274
00:31:37,734 --> 00:31:40,328
Salamander hurls his chain!

275
00:31:44,341 --> 00:31:46,719
Black Tiger is wrapped up!

276
00:31:46,743 --> 00:31:48,734
He's on the chopping block!

277
00:32:23,907 --> 00:32:26,386
The Tiger Back Breaker!

278
00:32:26,410 --> 00:32:28,888
He killed in a split second!

279
00:32:28,912 --> 00:32:30,690
If you blinked, you missed it!

280
00:32:30,714 --> 00:32:32,692
Our exceptionally talented rookie

281
00:32:32,716 --> 00:32:34,810
brought down the house!

282
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:40,600
I made good money. I appreciate your work.

283
00:32:40,624 --> 00:32:42,602
My pleasure.

284
00:32:42,626 --> 00:32:46,585
I can see that the Tokyo Office is in good hands.

285
00:32:46,697 --> 00:32:48,875
Of course.

286
00:32:48,899 --> 00:32:50,777
A talent like the Black Tiger

287
00:32:50,801 --> 00:32:53,479
comes around only once in a decade.

288
00:32:53,503 --> 00:32:55,582
You've found someone

289
00:32:55,606 --> 00:32:59,986
worthy of wearing the masks you invented.

290
00:33:00,010 --> 00:33:03,189
I'm still improving them.

291
00:33:03,213 --> 00:33:06,793
The question is whether the guys

292
00:33:06,817 --> 00:33:08,911
can keep up as the masks evolve.

293
00:33:30,507 --> 00:33:33,686
In your current shape,

294
00:33:33,710 --> 00:33:37,704
you can fight at full force only for a limited time.

295
00:33:38,916 --> 00:33:41,394
If it stays on too long,

296
00:33:41,418 --> 00:33:45,412
your body will begin
to deteriorate from the inside.

297
00:33:48,225 --> 00:33:50,970
Know the limit of your mask

298
00:33:50,994 --> 00:33:53,190
and fight accordingly.

299
00:34:05,208 --> 00:34:08,109
You always make the same moves.

300
00:34:09,513 --> 00:34:13,192
You lucked out this time.

301
00:34:13,216 --> 00:34:14,994
When is your debut match?

302
00:34:15,018 --> 00:34:17,597
Next week.

303
00:34:17,621 --> 00:34:18,998
Good luck.
Thanks.

304
00:34:19,022 --> 00:34:23,016
How much did you make? Show it to me.

305
00:34:27,798 --> 00:34:30,199
Look at this wad of cash!

306
00:34:32,602 --> 00:34:35,982
So, what's next?

307
00:34:36,006 --> 00:34:39,601
We're gonna party all the way with this money!

308
00:35:19,416 --> 00:35:21,407
Here you are.

309
00:35:27,024 --> 00:35:29,425
Enjoy your meal.

310
00:35:41,316 --> 00:35:44,115
Hey, look at that.

311
00:36:17,719 --> 00:36:19,496
Hi.

312
00:36:19,520 --> 00:36:22,599
Let's go.

313
00:36:22,623 --> 00:36:25,002
Cold shoulder, right?

314
00:36:25,026 --> 00:36:27,017
Naoto, come on.

315
00:36:28,930 --> 00:36:31,024
Naoto.

316
00:36:34,736 --> 00:36:36,914
Would you like a drink?

317
00:36:36,938 --> 00:36:39,183
Me?

318
00:36:39,207 --> 00:36:41,185
Dan!

319
00:36:41,209 --> 00:36:44,888
Bourbon on the rocks.

320
00:36:44,912 --> 00:36:47,291
Me too.

321
00:36:47,315 --> 00:36:49,010
All right.

322
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:55,321
Here you go.

323
00:36:56,624 --> 00:36:59,321
Cheers!

324
00:37:05,833 --> 00:37:07,411
Are you okay?

325
00:37:07,435 --> 00:37:09,413
Don't mock me!

326
00:37:09,437 --> 00:37:10,514
Another one.

327
00:37:10,538 --> 00:37:12,583
We've got juice, if you want.

328
00:37:12,607 --> 00:37:13,784
We've got juice.

329
00:37:13,808 --> 00:37:17,087
Shut up! Just give me another one.

330
00:37:17,111 --> 00:37:19,808
Me too.

331
00:37:32,683 --> 00:37:34,361
How old are you?

332
00:37:34,385 --> 00:37:35,978
How about you, baby?

333
00:38:43,811 --> 00:38:46,590
What are you doing here?

334
00:38:46,614 --> 00:38:50,561
Show me how the Black Tiger fights.

335
00:38:50,384 --> 00:38:52,284
What did you say?

336
00:39:03,797 --> 00:39:05,788
Let go of me!

337
00:39:12,406 --> 00:39:14,384
If you wanna fight him,

338
00:39:14,408 --> 00:39:16,686
you've gotta fight me first.

339
00:39:16,710 --> 00:39:18,588
Pardon me.

340
00:39:18,612 --> 00:39:20,603
Take it outside, will you?

341
00:39:25,686 --> 00:39:28,587
I'll get you first, as you wish.

342
00:39:30,490 --> 00:39:32,686
Better be ready for me.

343
00:39:35,495 --> 00:39:37,987
Could you please leave?

344
00:39:41,802 --> 00:39:45,081
I can't wait for my match next week.

345
00:39:45,105 --> 00:39:48,084
Next time I'll buy you drinks.

346
00:39:48,108 --> 00:39:50,587
Naoto.

347
00:39:50,611 --> 00:39:52,488
Hey, are you listening?

348
00:39:52,512 --> 00:39:55,692
Stop!

349
00:39:55,716 --> 00:39:58,962
Naoto! Hey!

350
00:39:58,986 --> 00:40:01,464
Keep the change.

351
00:40:01,488 --> 00:40:03,166
Naoto.
This is it.

352
00:40:03,190 --> 00:40:05,284
What's going on?

353
00:40:10,898 --> 00:40:12,798
What are you looking at?

354
00:40:17,204 --> 00:40:21,198
I was raised here.

355
00:40:24,711 --> 00:40:27,112
Here?

356
00:40:35,389 --> 00:40:37,881
Why are you hiding?

357
00:40:47,501 --> 00:40:51,481
Ruriko.

358
00:40:51,505 --> 00:40:55,485
Mercy is for the weak.

359
00:40:55,509 --> 00:40:59,503
Fairness is the excuse of fools.

360
00:41:02,115 --> 00:41:04,777
For the glory of the Tiger's Lair.

361
00:41:09,990 --> 00:41:13,369
Naoto.

362
00:41:13,393 --> 00:41:16,385
You're thinking about that girl, aren't you?

363
00:41:18,999 --> 00:41:21,978
Ruriko...

364
00:41:22,002 --> 00:41:23,980
Ruriko, wasn't it?

365
00:41:24,004 --> 00:41:29,085
It's been 10 years and you still remembered.

366
00:41:29,109 --> 00:41:34,090
I knew it was her the minute I saw her face.

367
00:41:34,114 --> 00:41:36,310
Was she your first love?

368
00:41:38,986 --> 00:41:40,863
She wouldn't remember me, though.

369
00:41:40,887 --> 00:41:46,069
Of course not. You and I have changed too.

370
00:41:46,093 --> 00:41:49,372
So, Dan...
Here's 250-pound

371
00:41:49,396 --> 00:41:51,574
Super Kong of the Dragon's Lair
with 5 wins and one loss,

372
00:41:51,598 --> 00:41:55,478
He's ready to fight!

373
00:41:55,502 --> 00:41:58,494
I've gotta go.

374
00:42:01,108 --> 00:42:02,185
Don't lose.

375
00:42:02,209 --> 00:42:04,087
Of course not!

376
00:42:04,111 --> 00:42:06,689
I already have a plan for

377
00:42:06,713 --> 00:42:08,807
how to spend the money after the match.

378
00:42:12,586 --> 00:42:16,566
Don't steal my signature attack.

379
00:42:16,590 --> 00:42:19,769
What is it?

380
00:42:19,711 --> 00:42:22,203
The Tiger's Lair Plug.

381
00:42:50,909 --> 00:42:52,486
This is the debut match

382
00:42:52,510 --> 00:42:54,789
for the challenger from the Tiger's Lair.

383
00:42:54,813 --> 00:42:57,291
I'm not into this kind of stuff.

384
00:42:57,315 --> 00:43:00,094
Hey! This is the Tiger Mask!

385
00:43:00,118 --> 00:43:01,796
Awesome!

386
00:43:01,820 --> 00:43:05,800
Watch this!
What's this?

387
00:43:05,824 --> 00:43:07,301
Is it live?

388
00:43:07,325 --> 00:43:10,204
Gold Tiger grabs his legs!

389
00:43:10,228 --> 00:43:13,407
Here it comes! Giant Swing!

390
00:43:13,431 --> 00:43:17,678
He's spinning the giant Kong
with incredible speed!

391
00:43:17,702 --> 00:43:19,680
Kong is totally disoriented!

392
00:43:19,704 --> 00:43:22,583
It's a human centrifuge!

393
00:43:22,607 --> 00:43:27,188
Now Kong is thrown to the ropes!

394
00:43:27,212 --> 00:43:30,409
He bounces back! What's the next attack?

395
00:43:34,219 --> 00:43:35,997
It's the Lariat!

396
00:43:36,021 --> 00:43:39,500
It's explosive! He's going flying!

397
00:43:39,524 --> 00:43:43,304
Super Kong is airborne!

398
00:43:43,328 --> 00:43:45,506
It's a total knock-out!

399
00:43:45,530 --> 00:43:48,909
Gold Tiger earns an amazing victory,

400
00:43:48,889 --> 00:43:51,051
winning his debut match!

401
00:44:05,673 --> 00:44:07,951
Gold Tiger is responding

402
00:44:07,975 --> 00:44:10,354
to the roaring cheers in the house!

403
00:44:10,378 --> 00:44:13,156
He has a bright future ahead of him

404
00:44:13,180 --> 00:44:15,774
as a professional wrestler!

405
00:44:25,130 --> 00:44:26,207
What is happening here?

406
00:44:26,231 --> 00:44:29,510
White Tiger Mask bursts into the ring!

407
00:44:29,534 --> 00:44:31,412
What in the world...

408
00:44:31,436 --> 00:44:32,914
Is it a family feud?

409
00:44:32,938 --> 00:44:35,216
That idiot!

410
00:44:35,240 --> 00:44:40,121
This is unbelievable! The crowd is on fire!

411
00:44:40,145 --> 00:44:42,523
Kill him...
Kill him?

412
00:44:42,547 --> 00:44:45,847
The crowd is calling out, 'kill him!"

413
00:44:49,054 --> 00:44:53,634
How will Gold Tiger handle White Tiger's challenge?

414
00:44:53,658 --> 00:44:56,637
He's completely drained from the match!

415
00:44:56,661 --> 00:44:58,527
What the...

416
00:45:01,933 --> 00:45:03,833
You asked for this.

417
00:45:06,038 --> 00:45:08,716
I'll take you on first.

418
00:45:08,704 --> 00:45:10,082
Jerk...
Unbelievable!

419
00:45:10,106 --> 00:45:12,598
They rang the second bell!

420
00:45:17,613 --> 00:45:19,206
Too slow.

421
00:45:21,817 --> 00:45:24,296
Is that all you've got?

422
00:45:24,320 --> 00:45:25,719
Darn it!

423
00:45:47,040 --> 00:45:50,420
My body...

424
00:45:50,444 --> 00:45:53,122
Is that it?

425
00:45:53,146 --> 00:45:55,725
What a dirty trick!

426
00:45:55,749 --> 00:45:58,548
Fairness is the excuse of fools.

427
00:46:26,346 --> 00:46:28,124
Dan!

428
00:46:28,148 --> 00:46:31,327
What perfect timing!

429
00:46:31,351 --> 00:46:33,445
Hey! Leave him alone!

430
00:46:43,912 --> 00:46:46,210
Jo! Stop it!

431
00:46:47,816 --> 00:46:49,394
Stop!

432
00:46:49,418 --> 00:46:50,908
Dan!

433
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:53,415
Hang in there!

434
00:47:07,993 --> 00:47:11,238
Dan! Get up!

435
00:47:11,262 --> 00:47:14,254
Get up! Dan!

436
00:47:24,175 --> 00:47:26,053
Get up!

437
00:47:26,077 --> 00:47:28,255
Dan! Get up!

438
00:47:28,279 --> 00:47:33,260
Dan...

439
00:47:33,284 --> 00:47:35,582
You're just a big talker.

440
00:47:44,963 --> 00:47:48,160
Dan!

441
00:47:53,705 --> 00:47:56,383
I don't need any other Tiger Mask.

442
00:47:56,407 --> 00:48:00,105
It's not fair! The match is over!

443
00:48:02,413 --> 00:48:04,711
Let go!

444
00:48:06,517 --> 00:48:09,418
Stop...

445
00:48:33,311 --> 00:48:35,712
We don't think so!

446
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:39,611
I'll take you on later.

447
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:43,217
Darn it!

448
00:48:47,025 --> 00:48:49,824
Stay out of this!

449
00:48:58,002 --> 00:48:59,780
A German suplex to finish him off!

450
00:48:59,804 --> 00:49:02,082
It's fatal!

451
00:49:17,922 --> 00:49:21,916
Cold-blooded, bad-ass White Tiger rules!

452
00:49:23,428 --> 00:49:25,706
Dan, hang in there!

453
00:49:25,730 --> 00:49:28,008
Dan!

454
00:49:28,032 --> 00:49:31,312
Naoto...

455
00:49:31,336 --> 00:49:34,215
Sorry.

456
00:49:34,239 --> 00:49:36,717
I can't buy you a drink tonight.

457
00:49:36,741 --> 00:49:38,334
Don't worry.

458
00:49:40,712 --> 00:49:42,703
I'll go get a doctor.

459
00:49:46,317 --> 00:49:52,099
Your knee is completely shattered.

460
00:49:52,123 --> 00:49:55,102
Any pain?

461
00:49:55,126 --> 00:49:57,805
I'm all right.

462
00:49:57,829 --> 00:49:59,006
I'm sorry.

463
00:49:59,030 --> 00:50:01,809
No worries.

464
00:50:01,833 --> 00:50:05,827
You're finished as a fighter.

465
00:50:37,936 --> 00:50:39,927
It's the loser's fate.

466
00:50:45,043 --> 00:50:48,589
If you cross me again,

467
00:50:48,613 --> 00:50:50,911
you're going to die.

468
00:51:04,829 --> 00:51:06,607
No...

469
00:51:06,631 --> 00:51:08,909
This can't be!

470
00:51:08,933 --> 00:51:11,912
Hey, Dan!

471
00:51:11,936 --> 00:51:14,815
You were alive a moment ago!

472
00:51:14,839 --> 00:51:17,418
Calm down.

473
00:51:17,442 --> 00:51:19,887
You've gotta be kidding!

474
00:51:19,911 --> 00:51:21,388
Wake up, Dan!

475
00:51:21,412 --> 00:51:24,211
Open your eyes, Dan!

476
00:52:51,936 --> 00:52:54,530
I'm not scheduled to see you today.

477
00:53:01,612 --> 00:53:08,295
What happened to Dan in the dressing room?

478
00:53:08,319 --> 00:53:10,811
Please tell me the truth.

479
00:53:12,523 --> 00:53:14,719
The truth?

480
00:53:16,727 --> 00:53:20,721
Have you seen a race horse with a broken leg?

481
00:53:22,333 --> 00:53:26,013
It is totally useless.

482
00:53:26,037 --> 00:53:30,634
Ending its life is the best option for both parties.

483
00:53:33,311 --> 00:53:36,090
Dan wasn't an animal.

484
00:53:36,114 --> 00:53:37,591
He was a human being.

485
00:53:37,615 --> 00:53:41,095
He wasn't just human.

486
00:53:41,119 --> 00:53:43,497
He was a fighter too.

487
00:53:43,521 --> 00:53:48,322
A fighter who cannot fight is not worthy of living.

488
00:53:50,728 --> 00:53:53,907
You can't really mean that.

489
00:53:53,931 --> 00:53:57,111
Tell me, Black Tiger Mask,

490
00:53:57,135 --> 00:54:00,514
why do you fight?

491
00:54:00,538 --> 00:54:02,416
I...

492
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:05,219
An enormous amount of money

493
00:54:05,243 --> 00:54:07,788
moves behind the scenes at those matches.

494
00:54:07,812 --> 00:54:10,491
The Tiger's Lair is spread throughout the world.

495
00:54:10,515 --> 00:54:14,509
We use the money from the matches
to rule the Underworld.

496
00:54:16,521 --> 00:54:20,014
And you fight to earn money.

497
00:54:30,935 --> 00:54:36,339
I'm sorry that you lost your friend.

498
00:54:38,743 --> 00:54:40,802
It pains me too.

499
00:54:43,214 --> 00:54:45,808
Take as much as you want.

500
00:54:48,119 --> 00:54:50,213
Have fun for a change.

501
00:54:58,829 --> 00:55:02,823
Thank you very much...

502
00:55:04,936 --> 00:55:08,415
for waking me up.

503
00:55:08,439 --> 00:55:10,840
What are you saying?

504
00:55:38,035 --> 00:55:41,615
Why do you think

505
00:55:41,639 --> 00:55:44,518
I clothed an orphan like you,

506
00:55:44,542 --> 00:55:49,503
fed you and trained you
to become the greatest fighter?

507
00:55:50,915 --> 00:55:54,094
If you choose to be ungrateful

508
00:55:54,118 --> 00:55:57,418
and walk out the door for good,

509
00:55:59,724 --> 00:56:05,105
I'll hunt you down no matter where you go.

510
00:56:05,129 --> 00:56:10,124
And you'll pay for it with your own life.

511
00:56:13,237 --> 00:56:15,228
Make a wise decision.

512
00:56:29,020 --> 00:56:32,217
I don't belong here anymore.

513
00:57:00,217 --> 00:57:02,396
How was it in Europe?

514
00:57:02,420 --> 00:57:07,401
Berlin, Paris, Rotterdam.

515
00:57:07,425 --> 00:57:09,803
Each branch has promising talent.

516
00:57:09,827 --> 00:57:14,608
I see. Where are you going next?

517
00:57:14,632 --> 00:57:19,513
I'll stop in Hawaii and the U.S. mainland.

518
00:57:19,537 --> 00:57:21,615
I expect a thorough search.

519
00:57:21,639 --> 00:57:24,540
The Tokyo Branch might be going downhill.

520
00:57:27,111 --> 00:57:29,512
I understand, sir.

521
00:57:42,326 --> 00:57:43,804
Ouch!

522
00:57:43,828 --> 00:57:47,128
He woke up! The bum is up!

523
00:57:51,135 --> 00:57:53,113
Trespassing is not allowed.

524
00:57:53,137 --> 00:57:54,935
Please leave.

525
00:57:57,441 --> 00:57:58,719
I'll call the police.

526
00:57:58,743 --> 00:58:01,713
I'm sorry. Somehow I ended up here.

527
00:58:05,416 --> 00:58:07,194
What's going on?

528
00:58:07,218 --> 00:58:09,996
Ruriko.

529
00:58:10,020 --> 00:58:12,114
And you are...

530
00:58:13,724 --> 00:58:15,818
Naoto?

531
00:58:35,813 --> 00:58:39,113
Hey, let's go outside.

532
00:58:42,520 --> 00:58:45,499
Hey mister, what are you doing here?

533
00:58:45,523 --> 00:58:48,015
Mister? Me?

534
00:58:50,628 --> 00:58:53,106
He's not a stray cat.

535
00:58:53,130 --> 00:58:55,208
He's a grown man.

536
00:58:55,232 --> 00:58:57,611
He should take care of himself.

537
00:58:57,635 --> 00:59:00,013
Just for a little while.

538
00:59:00,037 --> 00:59:03,517
We used to live together, you know.

539
00:58:47,028 --> 00:58:51,275
But he ran away and caused many problems!

540
00:58:51,299 --> 00:58:56,480
Dad was so worried, he lost half his hair.

541
00:58:56,504 --> 00:58:59,082
He was lost for 10 years, but now he's back?

542
00:58:59,106 --> 00:59:01,598
Sounds fishy.

543
00:59:03,411 --> 00:59:05,989
He might've escaped from prison.

544
00:59:06,013 --> 00:59:08,311
He's not like that.

545
00:59:14,221 --> 00:59:16,099
Kick the ball!

546
00:59:16,123 --> 00:59:18,421
Oh, man!

547
00:59:22,530 --> 00:59:26,076
Over here! Give me the ball!

548
00:59:26,100 --> 00:59:30,681
It's not like we have enough hands around here.

549
00:59:30,705 --> 00:59:33,383
Maybe he can work here,

550
00:59:33,407 --> 00:59:37,207
but only if he wants to.

551
00:59:44,118 --> 00:59:46,396
Taking care of kids

552
00:59:46,420 --> 00:59:50,414
is more than just playing with them.

553
00:59:54,328 --> 00:59:57,174
But, I guess...

554
00:59:57,198 --> 01:00:01,192
He can work for room and board.

555
01:00:03,404 --> 01:00:04,599
Thank you, brother.

556
01:00:13,914 --> 01:00:15,892
Oh, no.

557
01:00:15,916 --> 01:00:17,494
You're doing it wrong.

558
01:00:17,493 --> 01:00:21,273
Let me show you. Like this.

559
01:00:21,297 --> 01:00:23,775
We're home!

560
01:00:23,799 --> 01:00:26,378
All right. Got it.

561
01:00:26,402 --> 01:00:28,803
Keep it up.

562
01:00:38,180 --> 01:00:41,775
Manabu had an accident! He peed!

563
01:01:50,472 --> 01:01:55,553
I remember when you broke
dad's favorite fishing rod.

564
01:01:55,577 --> 01:01:58,356
<i>Really?
Yest</i>

565
01:01:58,380 --> 01:02:00,258
I don't remember.

566
01:02:00,282 --> 01:02:01,359
Come on...

567
01:02:01,383 --> 01:02:04,762
The house looks far better than

568
01:02:04,786 --> 01:02:08,666
what it used to be back then.

569
01:02:08,690 --> 01:02:14,539
It must've been very hard for my dad.

570
01:02:14,563 --> 01:02:19,344
Now I know.

571
01:02:19,368 --> 01:02:21,962
Your smile hasn't changed at all.

572
01:02:25,874 --> 01:02:27,968
Really?

573
01:02:30,879 --> 01:02:32,472
So, Naoto...

574
01:02:33,882 --> 01:02:36,060
Where have you been

575
01:02:36,084 --> 01:02:38,576
and what were you doing all this time?

576
01:02:44,359 --> 01:02:48,239
I was...

577
01:02:48,263 --> 01:02:52,043
working at a zoo.

578
01:02:51,741 --> 01:02:54,920
The face you make
when you lie hasn't changed, either.

579
01:02:54,944 --> 01:02:56,422
It's not a lie.

580
01:02:56,446 --> 01:02:59,024
A rich gentleman took care of me.

581
01:02:59,048 --> 01:03:03,529
And I worked at his zoo.

582
01:03:03,553 --> 01:03:06,932
But we had a fight recently and [ left.

583
01:03:06,956 --> 01:03:09,435
What is the zoo called?

584
01:03:09,459 --> 01:03:11,437
Tiger's Lair.

585
01:03:11,461 --> 01:03:13,739
Tiger's Lair?

586
01:03:13,763 --> 01:03:15,507
What is that?

587
01:03:15,531 --> 01:03:17,609
I've never heard of such a zoo!

588
01:03:17,633 --> 01:03:20,227
It's in the middle of nowhere.

589
01:03:31,948 --> 01:03:33,746
Let's get going.

590
01:03:39,255 --> 01:03:42,334
Well, Christmas is coming up.

591
01:03:42,358 --> 01:03:44,737
Is there anything you want?

592
01:03:44,761 --> 01:03:47,339
Let's see...

593
01:03:47,363 --> 01:03:49,832
A backpack. Manabu needs one for school.

594
01:03:56,038 --> 01:04:00,839
You are the only Tiger Mask left.

595
01:04:19,162 --> 01:04:22,325
Give me your blessing to fight him.

596
01:04:54,664 --> 01:04:59,211
Hey, everyone! Dinner time! Come back in!

597
01:04:59,235 --> 01:05:01,033
Wash your hands!

598
01:05:01,938 --> 01:05:05,340
Slow down! No need to push!

599
01:05:09,145 --> 01:05:11,637
Remember to gargle too!

600
01:05:15,751 --> 01:05:19,153
"Merry Christmas”

601
01:05:27,163 --> 01:05:29,530
Naoto!

602
01:06:03,733 --> 01:06:06,111
Watch out for the hook.

603
01:06:06,135 --> 01:06:10,129
Throw this over there, and the fish will bite.

604
01:06:34,664 --> 01:06:36,928
So, Naoto...

605
01:06:38,534 --> 01:06:42,314
What's your plan for the future?

606
01:06:42,338 --> 01:06:44,636
For my future?

607
01:06:47,243 --> 01:06:49,922
Only if you want...

608
01:06:49,946 --> 01:06:53,225
Why don't you work full time for us?

609
01:06:53,249 --> 01:06:55,445
Maybe get certified?

610
01:06:59,255 --> 01:07:02,054
Think about it seriously, will you?

611
01:07:08,564 --> 01:07:09,929
Thank you.

612
01:07:20,543 --> 01:07:24,222
Naoto! We caught one!

613
01:07:24,246 --> 01:07:27,926
Are you sure?
Yeah! I'm positive!

614
01:07:27,950 --> 01:07:29,127
Let me see.

615
01:07:29,151 --> 01:07:31,643
See? I'm reeling it in!

616
01:07:48,537 --> 01:07:51,336
Excuse me. Pardon me.

617
01:07:53,042 --> 01:07:55,921
Are you all right? Do we have everyone?

618
01:07:55,945 --> 01:07:59,624
Mr. Akira went in to get Manabu!

619
01:07:59,648 --> 01:08:03,228
Akira did?

620
01:08:03,252 --> 01:08:04,429
There he is!

621
01:08:04,453 --> 01:08:08,133
Are you okay?

622
01:08:08,157 --> 01:08:10,335
Yeah, we're all safe.

623
01:08:10,359 --> 01:08:13,839
Thank goodness, but what happened?

624
01:08:13,863 --> 01:08:16,308
I don't know the cause, but...

625
01:08:16,332 --> 01:08:20,312
One of the kids saw a stranger
when the fire broke out.

626
01:08:20,336 --> 01:08:22,814
Stranger?

627
01:08:22,838 --> 01:08:26,832
A tall man with a beard, I heard.

628
01:08:29,745 --> 01:08:32,942
Let's go.
Everyone, we need to get away.

629
01:08:37,353 --> 01:08:39,151
Naoto!

630
01:09:42,690 --> 01:09:44,988
I've been waiting for you.

631
01:09:50,898 --> 01:09:56,359
You had the Children's Home
set on fire, didn't you?

632
01:09:59,373 --> 01:10:02,052
You sent him.

633
01:10:02,076 --> 01:10:06,070
You broke the rule of the Tiger's Lair.

634
01:10:06,280 --> 01:10:12,362
But if you beg for mercy, I may forgive you.

635
01:10:12,386 --> 01:10:17,085
Mercy is for the weak.

636
01:10:19,393 --> 01:10:22,488
Isn't that right?

637
01:10:33,774 --> 01:10:37,053
I raised you like my son

638
01:10:37,077 --> 01:10:40,557
and gave you power and wisdom.

639
01:10:40,581 --> 01:10:44,060
But you got lost in your feelings?

640
01:10:44,084 --> 01:10:48,078
And you couldn't become strong in the true sense.

641
01:10:49,690 --> 01:10:51,488
What a shame!

642
01:10:55,095 --> 01:10:57,996
Power and wisdom mean nothing...

643
01:11:00,901 --> 01:11:03,246
if your heart is lost.

644
01:11:03,270 --> 01:11:06,171
You can't call that strong!

645
01:11:29,105 --> 01:11:31,784
You killed my best friend.

646
01:11:31,808 --> 01:11:34,402
And you robbed the children of their home.

647
01:11:36,379 --> 01:11:39,679
I won't let you go on like this!

648
01:12:11,781 --> 01:12:14,760
He's turned against the Tiger's Lair.

649
01:12:14,784 --> 01:12:17,685
Great Tiger, kill off this fool.

650
01:12:21,090 --> 01:12:23,684
Great Tiger?

651
01:15:07,207 --> 01:15:09,198
You are finished.

652
01:15:11,511 --> 01:15:15,209
Everything you have is now mine to destroy.

653
01:15:18,118 --> 01:15:22,098
Not only your life...

654
01:15:22,122 --> 01:15:25,524
But the girl and all those little children.

655
01:15:38,380 --> 01:15:40,781
No, you won't!

656
01:15:43,885 --> 01:15:45,979
It's time for you to wake up!

657
01:16:50,181 --> 01:16:51,876
Mr. X...

658
01:16:55,086 --> 01:17:00,183
Give me more power.

659
01:17:12,069 --> 01:17:13,366
Jo!

660
01:17:19,076 --> 01:17:22,055
I expected more from him.

661
01:17:22,079 --> 01:17:25,959
But it was too much for him.

662
01:17:25,983 --> 01:17:29,078
The newest mask went to waste.

663
01:17:46,470 --> 01:17:49,167
Jo...

664
01:18:02,887 --> 01:18:05,165
I won't forgive you!

665
01:18:05,189 --> 01:18:07,167
Never hurt anyone ever again!

666
01:18:07,191 --> 01:18:10,286
Farewell, Tiger Mask.

667
01:18:29,480 --> 01:18:31,881
Naoto!

668
01:18:38,489 --> 01:18:44,087
I know you will come back to me.

669
01:19:11,088 --> 01:19:13,767
Keep your guard up.

670
01:19:13,791 --> 01:19:16,370
This place will be closed.

671
01:19:16,394 --> 01:19:21,662
But the Tiger's Lair has
a network throughout the world.

672
01:19:27,892 --> 01:19:30,384
What will you do?

673
01:19:33,998 --> 01:19:36,399
I won't run away.

674
01:19:39,804 --> 01:19:42,296
I'll keep on fighting.

675
01:20:49,507 --> 01:20:51,908
Naoto.

676
01:21:11,596 --> 01:21:16,076
We need to buy a new one.

677
01:21:16,100 --> 01:21:18,000
It's my fault.

678
01:21:20,887 --> 01:21:25,768
I'm so sorry.

679
01:21:25,792 --> 01:21:28,571
Why is that?

680
01:21:28,595 --> 01:21:31,189
How is it your fault?

681
01:21:32,899 --> 01:21:35,561
I shouldn't have come back here.

682
01:21:42,339 --> 01:21:44,417
My dad...

683
01:21:44,441 --> 01:21:49,845
thought of you as his own son.

684
01:21:50,948 --> 01:21:54,942
He believed you'd come back
until the day he died.

685
01:21:57,955 --> 01:22:03,736
So, when you showed up,

686
01:22:03,760 --> 01:22:07,253
I was very happy.

687
01:22:12,611 --> 01:22:16,190
Thank you.

688
01:22:16,214 --> 01:22:19,694
You accepted me unconditionally.

689
01:22:19,254 --> 01:22:21,154
I appreciate that.

690
01:22:24,960 --> 01:22:30,262
I was so happy just being here.

691
01:22:39,374 --> 01:22:44,437
Are you leaving again?

692
01:22:54,256 --> 01:22:58,250
For the first time, I have someone I want to protect.

693
01:23:02,464 --> 01:23:04,660
That's why I'm leaving.

694
01:23:17,245 --> 01:23:18,940
Promise me...

695
01:23:22,250 --> 01:23:25,242
that you'll be back.

696
01:23:41,570 --> 01:23:45,249
I will because...

697
01:23:45,273 --> 01:23:47,367
this is my home.

699
01:25:37,152 --> 01:25:42,133
Don't ever think I'm done with you.

700
01:25:42,157 --> 01:25:44,057
Tiger Mask!

701
01:29:56,044 --> 01:29:59,823
Miss Ruriko. This is for you.

702
01:29:59,847 --> 01:30:01,941
Thank you.

703
01:30:12,360 --> 01:30:15,557
"To Miss Ruriko Wakatsuki,
Chibikko Children's Home"

704
01:30:20,868 --> 01:30:24,566
"Merry Christmas”
"10 million yen"

705
01:30:34,248 --> 01:30:39,743
"In honor of the sudden passing of Mr. Hisao Maki"